+# Attribution and scope
+
+Apache-2.0, under the repository license. This contribution was prepared with
+substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. It is an independent verification effort;
+no priority or improved integer-multiplication bound is claimed.
+
+The unchanged source word and geometry are inherited from the contributors
+credited in PR442 and its ancestors, including Dylan Crow (with Anthropic
+Claude assistance), Jacob Sussman, Zhihao Chen (with OpenAI Codex assistance),
+and the earlier source527/PR234/PR266/PR315/PR346/PR352/PR363 contributors.
+Their existing notices and repository history remain authoritative.
+
+The multiple-host algebra reuses the preceding local WholeHosting package.
+The gauge convention and partial-swap identities follow existing
+`research/machine-transfer-verification/transfer-proof/framed/FramedXor.lean`
+and `AddressGauges.lean` at pinned main. New adaptations explicitly separate
+generic simulation lemmas from concrete source instantiation.
+
+The refreshed audit also reviewed PR509 at
+`7b9c720ecc9f483c383e7cd9c2ab81f06ee5df59`, which formalizes the generic
+Lemma G frame-conjugation, replay, and bit-entrance principles. Those
+principles are overlapping existing work, not a novelty claim here. This
+package targets the additional literal PR442 event, frame, owner, and
+clean-private-register obligations. See `overlap-review.md`.
+
+The closing audit also reviewed PR513's sequential completed-bank theorem
+and five-stage source bindings at
+`005dd3f4e3cba8d1761abc4ab391aaf6d14d6f73`. Its generic completion algebra
+overlaps with this contribution's framework; it retains the physical
+arbitrary-dirty-input endpoint as a supplier premise. No novelty for generic
+completion algebra is claimed here.
+
+The input snapshots preserve the pinned generated source bytes. Compression
+of previously uncompressed JSON uses deterministic gzip; the uncompressed
+hashes identify the original files exactly. No source algorithm was changed.
+
+PR448's split-stream gain remains unestablished. Nothing here assumes its
+missing interface or supplies an uncharged additional register. This package
+does not establish a compiler, physical resource bill, asymptotic transfer,
+or unconditional integer-multiplication theorem.
