@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Actual original-bank ownership review
+
+The selected source is PR442 commit `4e16d001d505d4f21dd2bcfc44591f9be4c279bd`, stage 2, replica 0, pair 0, forward. The original parent template has 987 live local roles and private family 14259. Its uncompressed SHA256 is `f9ce9ac945d9e8ea737dc5e456e366a7e2a21d8b989d24b742d7f124d26fb32f`; the other vendored input hashes are in `source-versions.json`.
+
+`generate_parent_ownership.py` reads every selected original owner and the corresponding source entrance frame. Its 747 helpers occupy 172 original bank families. For each route it maps the sorted residual standard basis to the specified bank interval, then completes the coordinate permutation by the increasing bijection between the complements. This explicitly chooses an isometry satisfying the source's interval descriptor; the source descriptor does not specify the complementary-axis ordering. Parent helpers have no additional B-port family chart. Data roles use the same source stage 2 port charts as the hosted call, with inverse convention chosen so the owner chart is `d * rho`.
+
+There are 61 route slots but 59 distinct permutations. Three slots share the identity permutation: offset 0 / width 7 / frame 9, offset 0 / width 8 / frame 0, and offset 4 / width 4 / frame 458. The Lean tables keep slot metadata separate from permutation tags. Treating slots as distinct actions would have invalidated the function-injectivity proof.
+
+`ParentOwnershipData.lean` checks both permutation inverse laws, the source-to-bank support equation for all 61 slots and 64 axes, faithfulness of all 59 permutation tags, and the inverse owner lookup for all 987 roles. Each helper family is at least 7680 and below 14259; data families are 0 through 239. The tables regenerate byte for byte (SHA256 `737ae7eb42e3d287db5fcd840eecef3c80bc0e01238bba2c8ba8cfbd162c3220`). Their Lean4.33.0 kernel build took 114.2 seconds on this machine. The generic owner-injectivity and coordinate-chart proofs were separately compiled against these tables. The complete `ParentOwnership.lean` module then compiled in 1.6 seconds using the checked data and source port charts; its reported theorem closures contain only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. The package-wide replay supplies the final import check.
+
+`ParentOwnership.lean` derives injectivity of actual owner functions for any fixed invertible cover and field with 2 nonzero. Descriptor inequality alone is not an assumption. The private row is separated by its reserved family 14259. Every parent active owner avoids host families 240 through 7679. The full-word gather theorem and native-cover theorem instantiate the generic raw-word semantics with these actual charts; callers still supply the concrete event word and initial-state relation. The private identifier `(14259,id)` denotes reserved scratch, while its per-invocation native chart is explicitly the common cover d.
+
+JSON extraction and the interpretation of the upstream route descriptor are outside the Lean kernel. The kernel certifies the resulting literal table and its mathematical properties. These files establish no improved kappa, all-size compiler, or interface for PR448's disputed two-stream split.
